# A deposit holds only so many extractors, and a territory with none free refuses another.
#
# **There is no row saying zero.** A quantity of nothing is not written - Sean, 2026-09-15: *the
# model is a minimal expression of intent* - so a deposit with no capacity left is a deposit with
# no `free` row, and the refusal is the same one a missing border gives.
#
# **This is why capacity is not stated.** Building spends one free and arithmetic already refuses
# to take what is not there, so the limit needs nothing the engine cannot do.

{test name:an-extractor-cannot-be-built-with-no-free-capacity}

{given}
{territory id:1 name:territory-1}
{residency what:labor where:territory-1} -> 1
{residency what:metal where:territory-1} -> 1

{when}
{build-extractor where:territory-1 for:food}

{refused}
{free where:territory-1 what:food} -> 1
